ge (wGA) without CLD, and in infants at 32&#x02013;35 wGA without CLD (combined analysis). Data from Simoes [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B44">44</xref>].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rr187-1"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Hospitalization rates</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="center" colspan="2">Children &#x02264; 2 years old with BPD/CLD (<italic>n</italic> = 3675)</td><td align="center" colspan="2">Infants at gestational age 29&#x02013;32 weeks without CLD (<italic>n</italic> = 4854)</td><td align="center" colspan="2">Infants at gestational age 32&#x02013;35 weeks without CLD (<italic>n</italic> = 2829)</td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan="2"><hr></hr></td><td colspan="2"><hr></hr></td><td colspan="2"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Reference (country)</td><td align="center">Untreated</td><td align="center">Palivizumab</td><td align="center">Untreated</td><td align="center">Palivizumab</td><td align="center">Untreated</td><td align="center">Palivizumab</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B23">23</xref>] (USA)</td><td align="center">36.7% (30)</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td></tr><tr><td align="left">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B24">24</xref>] (USA)</td><td align="center">17.4% (149)</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td></tr><tr><td align="left">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B52">52</xref>] (USA)</td><td align="center">25.2% (131)</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">7.6% (662)</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td></tr><tr><td align="left">[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B53">53</xref>] (UK)</td><td align="center">19.1% (235)</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="center">-</td><td align="cen